Z||000005||Oreif||09-01-2000||12:46 AM||||I paid $50 for a set of 1984 notchback sail panels with the SE on them. The 1984 are glass. They won't crack or craze like the plastic ones. I see no reason why you couldn't fill the holes and paint them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-01-2000||12:18 PM||||do you mean the platic fasteners that hold the back of the pannel? You can replace those with off the shelf christmastree type fasteners for about a $1.50. The part # is in my cave or at the <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>site that sells replacment pannels.</A> He's got the pannels for allot less than $100.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||moonie||09-01-2000||01:59 PM||||i see where i made my mistake in what i was talking about.<BR>on mine (85 se ) the ' sail panel is actually 2 parts. <BR>first part has 2 snap in & also has a clip<BR>that covers whole in body.<BR>second part is the triangle plexiglass that <BR>has SE stuck on the other with what looks like double sided tape.<P>that was what i meand to ask do i need.<BR>but , since i went outside & removed <BR>the whole deal , i can see that the plexiglass is just cosmetic. <P>sorry for the confusion , & thanks <P>moonie <BR> <P>||||reg||1
